## Introduction & Basics

### What is C++?
- **Compiled Language**: Converted to machine code before execution
- **Statically Typed**: Type checking at compile time
- **Multi-paradigm**: Supports procedural, object-oriented, and functional programming
- **High Performance**: Close to hardware, minimal overhead
- **Standards**: C++98, C++03, C++11, C++14, C++17, C++20, C++23
- **Philosophy**: Zero-overhead abstractions, trust the programmer

### Key Characteristics
| Feature | Benefit |
|---------|---------|
| Direct memory access | Maximum control & performance |
| Manual memory management | Deterministic resource cleanup |
| Compile-time evaluation | No runtime overhead |
| Multiple inheritance | Flexible design patterns |
| Operator overloading | Expressive, readable code |
| Templates | Generic, reusable components |

