## Data Types & Variables

### Type System Theory

C++ uses a **static type system** where types are checked at compile time. This contrasts with:
- **Dynamic Languages** (Python, JavaScript): Type checking at runtime
- **Gradual Typing** (TypeScript): Mix of static and dynamic typing
- **Strong vs Weak Typing**: C++ is relatively weak (implicit conversions), Rust is very strong

**Type Safety Pyramid**:
```
Rust (Safest)
↓
C++ with modern practices
↓
Java/C#
↓
Python/JavaScript (Least safe, most flexible)
```

