## Functions

### Function Declaration & Definition

**Theory**: Functions are reusable blocks of code. C++ uses both declaration (prototype) and definition pattern:

```cpp
// Declaration (tells compiler function exists)
int add(int a, int b);

// Definition (actual implementation)
int add(int a, int b) {
    return a + b;
}

// Usage
int result = add(5, 3);  // result = 8

// Early return pattern
int divide(int a, int b) {
    if (b == 0) {
        return -1;  // Early exit for error case
    }
    return a / b;
}

// Multiple returns are possible but one is preferred
bool findValue(int arr[], int size, int target, int& result) {
    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
        if (arr[i] == target) {
            result = i;
            return true;
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```

